IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sk73-nouns`

-- Row il-73. THE REFERENCES, as typed values: two items (I1 and I2), the printed instructions and provisions they rest on, the enactments named by I1 with the status the deposited instruments give them, and the controls.
-- Tests of the controls are in sk73-tests-controls.l4, tests that pin the readings are in sk73-tests-readings.l4, and the assertions that FAIL on purpose (two, one per item) are in sk73-tests-red.l4.
--
-- THE QUOTATION LINES.
-- `src:N` lines are expanded mechanically from the excerpt of the Hebrew Wikisource consolidation (UNOFFICIAL, so CONSOLIDATION-ONLY) by tools/srcquote.py; N is the line number in the whole page, which the excerpt's header lists.
-- `ext:[tag]` lines quote the Hebrew read from the deposited page image of an official instrument; the tag names the issue and the printed page (shNNN-pPPP is Sefer HaChukim issue NNN, printed page PPP; dmi37-pPPP is the Dinei Medinat Israel new-version print 37, printed page PPPP). The images are in registers/source-bundle/pages/.
-- Nothing is quoted from memory. Every Hebrew string typed below as a token is a run copied from an ext: or src: line (tools/hebcheck.py checks it), and every date, number and section is on a quotation line or in NOTES.md.
-- Footnote numbers are left out of the quoted strings. Where a page prints a space before a colon or a semicolon, or a long dash where the line writes an en dash, the line writes it without the space or with the en dash (NOTES.md, fork F9).

§ `References`

